Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:05.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,There was a little café where Rahel and\NBekele met every Friday.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.76,0:00:09.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Rahel knew just how Bekele liked his\Ncoffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.57,0:00:16.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,When Rahel didn’t smile, Bekele knew a\Nhard day lay behind it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.24,0:00:19.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,But she never knew that he loved her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.73,0:00:24.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,One afternoon, Rahel told him she’d\Nfound a job in another city.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.21,0:00:28.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele smiled and said, “My hero, you\Nknow how proud I am of you.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.90,0:00:35.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,That night, Bekele typed, “There was\Nsomething I wanted to tell you.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.96,0:00:39.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then his thumb stopped over send.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.44,0:00:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,But he deleted the message.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.15,0:00:46.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was afraid that the truth coming out\Nmight change their friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.69,0:00:51.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,When they reached the bus station, Rahel\Nsaid she was scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.39,0:00:54.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele carried her bag and walked with\Nher.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.11,0:00:58.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Before she boarded the bus, she packed\Nhim a little coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.31,0:01:01.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,“So we don’t miss our Friday coffee,”\Nshe said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.98,0:01:08.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just as the bus pulled away, his phone\Nlit up: “Friday. Same as always?”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.69,0:01:12.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele smiled and typed, “I’ll be\Nthere.”
